				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for storage expansion and dialog fixes\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule from `feccffc3` to `1b955092` to synchronize the latest revisions for `Cocoon`, `Mountain`, and `Sky` on the Current branch.\n\n**Cocoon:** Introduce the `Storage.GetItems` RPC method to support bulk retrieval and refactor URI resolution logic to explicitly validate `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties, preventing malformed URIs during request routing.\n\n**Mountain:** Fix `ShowMessageBox` to correctly concatenate title and detail text for native dialog usability and correct `QuickInputShowQuickPick` to preserve multi-select return arrays. Remove the obsolete `showTextDocument` handler from IPC routing now that Sky handles this natively.\n\n**Sky:** Modify `BakeExtensionManifest` to detect and invalidate cache stubs with zero extension counts, preventing build hangs caused by stale empty records.\n\nThese changes ensure robust storage handling, accurate user dialog behavior, and reliable extension metadata generation during the bootstrap sequence.",
			"SHA": "0a4bde413b3dfbfe6ee987002d20304c6618f4a4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:17:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to stabilize Sky bridge initialization\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 7adf09f0 to feccffc3 to synchronize the latest stabilization of the Sky component layer.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to eliminate aggressive retry loops and forced UI state manipulation found in `InstallDiagnostics` and `InstallTreeView`. Replace complex exponential backoff logic and direct panel visibility overrides with synchronous execution and natural reactive lifecycle management. This ensures bridge layers register features immediately upon workbench bootstrap, assuming the initialization sequence is now stable.\n\nThese changes reduce bundle size, remove hidden asynchronous delays during feature activation, and ensure bridge logic remains strictly deterministic. Failed registrations now fail fast, improving error tracking transparency.",
			"SHA": "4eaea9578cfd5738136a3d0172b42385fb2aa53a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:13:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to streamline Sky bridge initialization\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `1a736c21` to `7adf09f0` to synchronize the latest stabilization of the editor's extension bridge layer.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to remove aggressive retry logic and polling loops found in `InstallInlineCompletions`, `InstallScm`, `InstallSearch`, and `InstallTreeView`. These complex mechanisms, designed to handle upstream instability, are replaced with direct service acquisition and synchronous execution. This change assumes the workbench bootstrap sequence is now stable, allowing bridge layers to register features immediately.\n\nThis simplification reduces bundle size, eliminates hidden asynchronous delays during feature activation, and ensures bridge logic remains strictly deterministic. Failed registrations now fail fast, making error tracking more transparent.",
			"SHA": "ab9cf5ffec7027c307ceaa09cd78c3c0de2e3f7b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:09:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for Sky diagnostic bridge refinement\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `8fe235bf` to `1a736c21` to revert brittle forced-initialization logic in the diagnostic bridge and align with the reactive data-driven model.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to replace the previous implementation in `InstallDiagnostics.ts`, which forcibly opened the Problems panel on every diagnostic batch. This change removes all `openView` calls, throttling mechanisms, and per-batch visibility checks.\n\nThe new implementation relies on `IMarkerService.changeOne` for state updates and allows `MarkersView` to manage visibility naturally. A single, one-time intervention is introduced to clear persisted `activeFile` filters if the panel is already visible upon diagnostic arrival. This resolves the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue caused by stale filters without forcing UI state changes.\n\nThese updates reduce IPC overhead, eliminate unnecessary side effects, and ensure diagnostic updates strictly follow the reactive lifecycle of the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "0035fccf8743954dd5d67dda3331b22b7bd7a28b"
		}
	],
